    genre: "story",
    title_kr: "돈 문제로 멀어진 친구",
    title_en: "A friendship that fell apart over money",
    body_kr: "친한 친구와 동업으로 작은 온라인 쇼핑몰을 시작했을 때만 해도 우리 우정은 절대 흔들리지 않을 거라 믿었다. 그러나 매출이 예상보다 낮아지면서 서로 투자한 돈과 노력에 대한 셈법이 조금씩 달라지기 시작했다. 누가 더 많이 일했는지, 누구의 판단이 잘못됐는지를 두고 쌓인 불만이 결국 큰 다툼으로 터져 나왔다. 사업을 정리하기로 하면서 우리는 서로 얼굴도 보지 않을 만큼 서먹해졌다. 시간이 한참 지난 뒤에야 나는 우정과 돈 문제를 뒤섞은 것 자체가 애초에 무리였다는 것을 인정하게 됐다. 최근 다시 연락이 닿아 조심스럽게 안부를 주고받고 있지만, 예전 같은 사이로 돌아가기까지는 시간이 더 필요할 것 같다.",
    body_en: "When my close friend and I started a small online shop together as business partners, I believed our friendship would never waver. But as sales turned out lower than expected, our calculations about the money and effort each of us had invested gradually began to diverge. Resentment built up over who had worked harder and whose judgment had been wrong, and it eventually erupted into a major fight. When we decided to shut the business down, we grew so distant we didn't even see each other's faces. It was only much later that I admitted mixing friendship with money had been a mistake from the start. Recently we've reconnected and cautiously exchange messages, but it seems it will take more time to return to the way things used to be.",
    questions: [
      { question_en: "What caused the friendship to fall apart?", options: ["A misunderstanding about a trip", "Disagreements over money and effort in a shared business", "A romantic rivalry", "Political disagreements"], answerIndex: 1 },
      { question_en: "What did the narrator later admit?", options: ["The business idea was bad", "Mixing friendship and money was a mistake", "The friend was never trustworthy", "They should never have met"], answerIndex: 1 },
    ],
